== FALSE DISCRIMINATOR: bare unshare(CLONE_NEWNS) ==
  native                                                     -> rc=-1 errno=1
  hermit run --tmp=/tmp --no-rcb-time --max-timeslice disabled -> rc=-1 errno=1
  ^ EPERM BOTH WAYS. Proves nothing about hermit.

== DISCRIMINATING: unprivileged user+mount unshare (what nix's sandbox does) ==
  native   unshare --mount --user --map-root-user            -> OK
  hermit   unshare --mount --user --map-root-user            -> EPERM (refused)

CONCLUSION: nix's sandboxed builder path unshares before every build, so
nix cannot run INSIDE hermit and build. The exec-builder seam is correct
BECAUSE it inverts the nesting: nix does its namespace work on the host and
execve's a builder that hermit then owns.
